  "tagline": "Tiny schema-less Rust search backend that returns object IDs, running in a few MB of RAM.",
  "description": "Sonic is a minimalist search backend written in Rust by Valerian Saliou for the Crisp messaging platform. Instead of storing documents, it indexes words to object IDs in RocksDB and answers queries with ID lists you then look up in your primary database, which keeps memory use to a few megabytes even for millions of objects. It speaks a simple TCP text protocol (Sonic Channel) and supports search, suggest/autocomplete and per-collection buckets. It is a good fit for fast autocomplete and basic keyword lookup, not for relevance-heavy or semantic search.",
